WEBVTT

00:13:58.327 --> 00:14:00.740
Surprisingly, many interviewers
were less concerned

00:14:00.764 --> 00:14:01.955
about skills for the job

00:14:01.979 --> 00:14:03.234
than fit with the culture.

00:14:03.258 --> 00:14:06.085
LR: These ideas of this cultural fit,
"Do you fit with me?"

00:14:06.109 --> 00:14:09.619
often overwhelmed people's assessments

00:14:09.643 --> 00:14:11.608
of people's abilities to do the job.

00:14:12.041 --> 00:14:13.369
Now it's important to note

00:14:13.393 --> 00:14:15.091
that when we think of cultural fit,

00:14:15.115 --> 00:14:17.369
we often hear about this
as a really great thing

00:14:17.393 --> 00:14:18.908
that can boost the productivity

00:14:18.932 --> 00:14:20.646
and profitability of organizations,

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.448
and it a hundred percent can do that

00:14:22.472 --> 00:14:24.755
if it is defined in a specific way.

00:14:25.947 --> 00:14:27.845
AG: The beneficial kind of cultural fit

00:14:27.869 --> 00:14:30.329
is not about who can swap
lacrosse stories with you,